# SKUEL direnv loader — secrets out of the worktree.
#
# The OS keychain (service "skuel") is the live credential source.
# `SKUEL_CREDENTIAL_BACKEND=keyring` (set in ./.env) makes `get_credential()` read
# the keychain FIRST and consult `os.getenv` only as a fallback, so nearly every
# credential the app resolves — session signing, LLM/embedding keys, the TEST_*
# passwords — is never exported into the shell at all. For the live inventory:
#   uv run python -c 'from core.config.credential_store import get_active_backend
#   print(get_active_backend().list_keys())'
# See core/config/credential_store.py.
#
# Loads:
#   1. ~/.config/skuel/secrets.env  → exactly two entries, each for a reason the
#                                     keychain cannot serve. NEO4J_AUTH is
#                                     env-only by necessity:
#                                     infrastructure/docker-compose.yml
#                                     interpolates `${NEO4J_AUTH}` and cannot
#                                     read a keychain (local sandbox only).
#                                     NEO4J_PASSWORD is a fallback copy of the
#                                     AuraDB password, kept so the app still
#                                     boots where libsecret cannot be unlocked
#                                     (headless / ssh). No other credential is
#                                     duplicated here — the keychain is the only
#                                     copy of the rest.
#                                     This file is OUTSIDE the worktree by
#                                     design — `git add .` cannot stage it.
#   2. ./.env                       → non-secret project config (NEO4J_URI,
#                                     APP_PORT, INTELLIGENCE_TIER, VAULT_ROOT…)
#                                     Still gitignored; safe to commit by
#                                     accident only because the pre-commit
#                                     secret-scan would catch credential
#                                     patterns even if it ever happened.
#
# Both files are loaded if present; missing files emit a soft direnv warning
# rather than failing.  Run `direnv allow` after editing this file.
#
# Migration / first-time setup:
#   uv run python scripts/migrate_secrets_to_keychain.py   # env file → keychain
#
# See: app/scripts/git-hooks/README.md
#      app/docs/roadmap/done/secrets-out-of-worktree.md

dotenv_if_exists ~/.config/skuel/secrets.env
dotenv_if_exists ./.env
